Achievement: 0 
Progress/Status: Update (September 2020)
================

PPPIA regulations have been approved. 

Update (March 2020)
==================

The PPPIA regulations are yet to be approved. ADB will continue liaising with the Office of Investment Board for possible engagement through the Office of Public Private Partnership. 

With regard to the financial completion of the project, pending payments have been released by the EA and the last withdrawal application has been processed. ADB has sent a letter to the EA requesting for refund of the outstanding balance of the advance account. All project related financial transactions are expected to completed by end-May 2020 allowing the project to financially close by Q2 2020. 

Update (January 2020)
==================
Project activities have been completed. Financial completion of the project is underway. 

The PPPIA regulations are yet to be approved. ADB held a mission of OPPP in November 2019 and will continue discussion with IBN to explore suitable opportunities for engagement. 


Update (October 2019) 
=================== 

ADB has approved a post-facto extension of the project from 31 July 2019 to 31 December 2019. ADB has also approved the cancellation of project savings of USD1 million as agreed with the government. 

The PPP regulations are being finalized. Strengthening of the PPP unit is expected over time, especially after the finalization of the organizational and management survey. 

The project earlier supported the preparation of several PPP-related guidelines and feasibility report of five potential PPP projects. Further work on supporting PPP-related activities will not be undertaken as agreed with the government. 

However, ADB is planning a mission (in November) from the Office of Public Private Partnership to discuss possible support for preparing PPP projects with the Office of Investment Board of Nepal (OIBN) . 

Update (June 2019)
============

PPPIA regulations have been drafted and is being processed for approval. Office of Investment Board of Nepal (OIBN) is analyzing the human resource requirement for the PPP Unit. 
Data Source: Reports from MOF, NRB, NPC, and SEBON

